==== OEM easy installation ====

As of vendor firmware 4.x flashing a vanilla OpenWrt from web interface does not work anymore. Both the configuration tool and the vendor modified Luci expect a tarball with some trailing JSON snippet and added checksums. I did not bother to fully understand the format of everything contained in the tarball and proceeded this way:

  - Update to the latest vendor supplied firmware. As of the writing on this section, this was 4.3.18, dated at 2024-08-13 which is based on OpenWrt 22.03.
  - Switch to the advanced configuration, aka Luci.
  - Set a password.
  - Enable SSH.
  - Login via SSH to flash the nor-nand-sysupgrade image using the sysupgrade CLI tool. I recommend to use -n option (do not keep configuration) to start over with a clean configuration.

This worked for me to upgrade from vendor version 4.3.18 (OpenWrt 22.03 based) to OpenWrt 24.10.0. Since you now have stock Luci, the next update should be possible from the web interface.


